a passenger plane split in two  after it overshot the runway and fell 35  feet  into a gorge many have died and scores  injured some in serious condition  the plane was carrying 190 people  including 10  infants and seven crew members  both the pilot and co-pilot have lost  their lives  the plane landed during the heavy  monsoon rain that has lashed the state  of  kerala over the last 24 hours  the air india express flight which was  coming in from dubai  and was landing in the kalikat airport  quasi-court airport  around 7 40 7 45  that seems to have skidded off the  runway and we must remember it's a  tabletop runway  so it seems to have crossed that runway  and fallen into a ditch sort of a place  pictures of the crash site show very  heavy damage to the plane's fuselage  and the front part of the aircraft the  ill-fated air india express  flight was a repatriation one regular  commercial flights have been halted in  india  because of the coronavirus outbreak  there are reports of the aircraft making  several rounds trying to land  it made two failed attempts  well one thing i think you'd clearly  want to look at as a factor would be the  weather conditions  so if you have a wet runway  it automatically increases the stopping  distance somewhat  if there is standing water there is a  possibility  of what's called aquaplaning where the  aircraft tyres never break through the  water layer  they're effectively water skiing rescue  operations are hindered  due to the heavy rainfall the civil  aviation ministry  has ordered an inquiry into the accident
 

